WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.270
A byte sets off down a cable: eight bits,

2
00:00:03.320 --> 00:00:04.950
zeros and ones.

3
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:08.070
Halfway along, there's a
crackle of interference.

4
00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:10.670
One bit flips from zero to one.

5
00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:14.690
What arrives is wrong, but it
looks just like any other byte.

6
00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:17.410
The receiver has never seen the original.

7
00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:19.630
So how could it possibly know?

8
00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:23.830
In this mission, you'll see how interference
during transmission can cause data

9
00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:27.050
loss, data gain or data change.

10
00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:30.990
You'll find out what really goes
wrong when bits travel down a wire.

11
00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:34.930
And you'll see how a sender
knows when it has to try again.

12
00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:39.360
Your mission: explain how a receiver
can tell that a bit has flipped.
